  "title": "Why Your CSV Total Is Wrong: 3 Data-Cleaning Bugs in Python",
  "description": "An 8-row fictional invoice CSV gives the wrong total when repeated invoices and hidden spaces are ignored. Watch actual Python running in a terminal as we inspect duplicate invoice IDs, normalize whitespace, use Decimal for accurate money calculations, save the cleaned CSV, and verify the output. Our fictional example changes the naive $2,656.25 total to $1,430.75 for six unique invoices. Check your own business rules before removing duplicate records; some repeated invoice keys can be legitimate. Original first-party demonstration and synthetic English narration, with no customer data or third-party footage.\n\nPython csv documentation: https://docs.python.org/3/library/csv.html\nPython decimal documentation: https://docs.python.org/3/library/decimal.html\n\n#Python #DataCleaning #FlowMinuteLab",
